    "id": "rate_half_ca_hankel_a1_first_degree_core_one_quadratic_gap_four_double_root_separated_center_overlap_cap_two",
    "title": "A=1 quadratic separated center-overlap cap two",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "exclusion of the four-scalar heavy-row overlap case",
    "statement": "In the separated double-root extremal profile, neither endpoint center alpha,beta can be a correction root: x_* lies outside their support union, so Q(gamma,x_*)=0 would make it padded and hence a common root of g_* and S_B. Thus at most theta is a correction center. At most one center is a root of g_* because the three-center rank-loss sum is at most one. Coprimality makes these disjoint, so j=deg gcd(Lambda,g_*S_B^2)<=2 and the heavy row has at most three free scalar coefficients.",
